cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use StaDE in your research, please cite it as below."
title: "StaDE: stability-aware differential expression and functional enrichment for public transcriptomes"
abstract: >-
  StaDE quantifies the reproducibility of differential-expression calls with a
  stratified bootstrap stability score and propagates that score into
  over-representation analysis, GSEA and gene-set selection frequency, so that
  enrichment conclusions require both statistical significance and replicability.
authors:
  - family-names: Lin
    given-names: Chenxi
version: 0.1.0
date-released: "2026-12-15"
license: MIT
type: software
keywords:
  - transcriptomics
  - differential expression
  - empirical Bayes
  - stability analysis
  - gene set enrichment
  - reproducibility
  - hepatocellular carcinoma
repository-code: "https://github.com/your-account/stade"
